title: Walking the cherry road: five photo tips
status: published
date: 2026-10-20 10:05
labels: photos
desc: Simple tips for beginners
comments: on
image: media/cherry.jpg
---
People ask how I take pictures, so here are the five things I do.

1. Shoot when the sun is low (morning, dusk)
2. Keep the horizon level
3. Put the road in the middle so the vanishing point shows
4. Take both landscape and portrait at each spot
5. Take many, with an eraser-like mind

> The last one is honestly the most important.

